# AI Adaptive Learning Platform — Core

## Product spine
Every feature must preserve: Source → Version → Section → Course Asset → Lineage → Sync Impact → Instructor Decision.

## Non-negotiables
- Instructor is final authority for published content. Never auto-publish AI output.
- Source versions are immutable. Never overwrite published source or content versions.
- Every generated asset MUST write `content_source_mapping` at generation time.
- Org isolation: Org A data must never leak to Org B.
- No dummy/stub domain logic in mergeable code — use interfaces + fakes only in tests.

## v1 scope lock
- PDF only. No DOCX/PPTX/HTML parsers.
- Assets: explanation + quiz only (structure chapters/topics allowed).
- Auth: simple mock roles (CONTENT_OWNER, INSTRUCTOR, STUDENT).
- Stack: Spring Boot, React, PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, S3/MinIO, OpenAI via AiProvider.

## Out of v1
Adaptive paths, multilingual, PPT/video, SSO, agents, three-way merge UI.

## Before coding a feature
1. Read the feature PRD under `docs/prds/`.
2. Implement against acceptance criteria + unit tests in that PRD.
3. Do not expand scope beyond the PRD.
